Version 0.3.0:
    * Object-oriented query API: PrologPredicate, PrologGoal, PrologQuery,
      PrologSolution, PrologVariable, PrologTerm, and PrologObject
    * Remove public string query API (query_text / call_predicate); use
      predicate(...).call(...) and solve(goal) instead
    * Lazy solve(): has_solution(), first(), iteration, all(), optional
      max_solutions cap, and PrologGoal.cut()
    * Process-global SWI-Prolog engine shared by all Prologot handles;
      cleanup() detaches without PL_cleanup() until extension unload
    * Shared prologot_boot.gd (create_engine, bundled res://bin/<os>/swipl)
    * GDScript facade, PrologotEngine autoload, named knowledge bases
      (create_knowledge_base / switch_knowledge_base with wipe)
    * PrologotNode scene node and PrologKnowledge Resource
    * expose_property / expose_method for explicit Godot ↔ Prolog bridges
    * Hybrid conversion policy: String → atom in, atom → String out,
      Prolog string → PrologTerm
    * Bundled SWI runtime copied into bin/<os>/swipl/ at build time;
      auto-detect home when initialize() omits "home"
    * Mini Dungeon demo (Prolog-driven goblin AI, nodes as Prolog terms)
    * Galactic Customs demo polish (atlas UI, briefing, gameplay fixes)
    * CI: reliable Windows/macOS builds, SWI DLL/@rpath fixes, ci_result.txt
      test gate, lint job (informational)
    * Documentation overhaul: glossary, getting started, API, installation,
      use cases, troubleshooting, prolog-developers
    * Expanded regression tests (facade, cut, knowledge bases, expose, lazy solve)

Version 0.2.0:
    * Generate GitHub artifacts for Godot asset lib

Version 0.1.0:
    * Initial commit
    * Working for Linux, not yet for MacOS and Windows
